# Command copyparty

## What does this command do:

Portable file server with accelerated resumable uploads, dedup, WebDAV, SFTP, FTP, TFTP, zeroconf, media indexer, thumbnails++ all in one file

## Installed from

For Fedora install using: curl -sSfL https://github.com/9001/copyparty/releases/download/v1.20.14/copyparty-sfx.py -o ~/.local/bin/copyparty && chmod +x ~/.local/bin/copyparty
For Raspberry Pi install using: curl -sSfL https://github.com/9001/copyparty/releases/download/v1.20.14/copyparty-sfx.py -o ~/.local/bin/copyparty && chmod +x ~/.local/bin/copyparty
For Mac install using: brew install copyparty

## Command path

For Fedora run: ~/.local/bin/copyparty
For Raspberry Pi run: ~/.local/bin/copyparty
For Mac run: /opt/homebrew/bin/copyparty

## Command documentation

Docs can be found at https://github.com/9001/copyparty

## Command options

# Serve current directory read/write (no auth)
copyparty

# Serve specific directory read-only
copyparty -v /path/to/files:/:r

# Serve with an account (user:pass) and read-write volume
copyparty -a user:pass -v /path/to/files:/:rw

# Listen on a specific port (default 3923)
copyparty -p 8080

# Listen on a specific IP
copyparty -i 0.0.0.0

# HTTP only (no TLS)
copyparty --http-only

# HTTPS only (auto-generates self-signed cert)
copyparty --https-only

# Add a config file
copyparty -c /path/to/config.ini

# Limit concurrent clients
copyparty -nc 50

# Use all CPU cores for uploads/downloads
copyparty -j 0

# Set server name (shown in browser top-left)
copyparty --name myserver

# Serve behind a reverse proxy at a sub-path
copyparty --rp-loc /files

# Show help
copyparty --help

# Volume flags (used with -v SRC:DST:FLAGS)
# r   = read-only
# rw  = read+write
# rwo = read+write+overwrite
# del = allow delete
# see: copyparty --help-accounts

# Protocol ports (defaults when enabled via config):
# HTTP:  3923  (configurable via -p)
# FTP:   3921
# SFTP:  3922
# TFTP:  3969
